\details{
goldfish consumes a \strong{single data object}: a \code{stocnet} (from the
\href{https://stocnet.github.io/manynet/}{\code{manynet}} package) that bundles the
node set, the network layers, and any attribute changes together. This page
is the reference for assembling that object with manynet's construction
verbs; the prebuilt \link{social_evolution} and \link{fisheries_treaties} datasets are
built exactly this way, and their help pages show the recipes end to end.
Once assembled, the object is passed straight to \code{\link[=estimate_dynam]{estimate_dynam()}},
\code{\link[=estimate_rem]{estimate_rem()}}, or \code{\link[=make_specification]{make_specification()}} as \code{data}, or gated early with
